  "rationale": "Recording-specific official evidence establishes the convening body: the City Secretary-posted agenda (retained-agenda) convenes the Planning and Zoning Commission WORK SESSION for Tuesday, January 18, 2022, and the Swagit player for recording 153032 (provider-player) carries the same official meeting title and identical agenda text; native-source-chapters mirrors the agenda items of the same recording. A work session is a meeting of the same commission, not a separate institution, so the body is the Addison Planning and Zoning Commission. The feed addison-tx-planning-and-zoning-commission ('Planning and Zoning Commission meetings for Addison') directly matches this convened body and its meetings, including work sessions. No joint conveners are proven; the agenda names no co-convening body. Venue (Addison TreeHouse), topics (plats, replats, zoning text amendment, annual report, work plan), staff presenter (Ken Schmidt, Director of Knowledge Services, presenting staff rather than a convening body), and references to the Regular Meeting do not create other institutional identities. Other supplied feeds (Board of Zoning Adjustment, City Council, Bond Committees, Community Partnership Committee, Comprehensive Plan Advisory Committee, Public Briefings, TIF, Public Input, UDC Advisory Committee) do not match the convened body under the identity policy. Ownership is fully proven, so no unresolved or unconfigured action is needed."
